 Melinda Jean Fan Lerwill MD           By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis  certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or  corrected the diagnosis       CLINICAL HISTORY  Left breast CA  positive margins  positive SNB  for reexcision and axillary  dissection     SPECIMENS SUBMITTED   A  BREAST RE EXCISION  LEFT  B  BREAST EXCISION FINAL MARGIN  LEFT LATERAL  C  BREAST EXCISION FINAL MARGIN  LEFT INFERIOR  D  LYMPH NODES DISSECTION  LEFT AXILLA    GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 4 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN     A  Received fresh  labeled  reexcision left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  fragmented piece of breast  The specimen is inked black  The specimen contains  a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm disrupted cavity with a smooth to nodular  hemorrhagic  surface and suture material as well as metallic clips  The surrounding tissue  consists of yellow white fibrofatty tissue  Representative sections  to include  the entire cavity  are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      B  Received fresh  labeled  final margin lateral  left breast   are three  pieces of breast  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The  specimen is inked black and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      C  Received fresh  labeled  final margin inferior   are two pieces of breast   measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm   REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The specimen is inked  black and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      D  Received fresh  labeled  left axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  piece of fat  which contains multiple lymph nodes  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE  cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  The largest possible lymph node vs  biopsy site has a  tan pink  focally friable and focally fibrotic cut surface  There is an  